      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Plack::Middleware::Session::Simple versions through 0.04 for Perl generates session ids insecurely.  The default session id generator returns a SHA-1 hash seeded with the built-in rand function, the epoch time, and the PID. The PID will come from a small set of numbers, and the epoch time may be guessed, if it is not leaked from the HTTP Date header. The built-in rand function is unsuitable for cryptographic usage.  Predicable session ids could allow an attacker to gain access to systems.  Plack::Middleware::Session::Simple is intended to be compatible with Plack::Middleware::Session, which had a similar security issue CVE-2025-40923.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
